12-round-half-even-pr-1", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 371137, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Ba9r4eQuPLMpo2GubxnR3p", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 372829, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer. I did not merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` imported and used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and `tests/test_money.py` (per FIN-212) expect `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Fix:** One line on branch `fix/round-half-even-fin-212` (commit `08d3cd5986`) switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Under that mode, 2.675 rounds to 2.68 and 2.665 rounds to 2.66, which matches the test.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the test and the implementation to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UPDZBXFiFGd6BbARZ63RCm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NvBvfGpYG4UvFp24kUndFN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The test expectations match ROUND_HALF_EVEN: 2.675 goes to 2.68 (7 is odd, so it rounds to the even 8) and 2.665 goes to 2.66. The implementation imports and uses ROUND_HALF_UP, which is the bug. I'll create a branch and make that one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HsSsrvYhneZsSJ1LYpKDio", "ca