but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, matching its docstring and FIN-212.\n\n## Verification\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: passed.\n\n## Notes\n- Changes one line in `src/money.py` (import and rounding mode). No other files touched.\n- Half-way cases now round to the nearest even cent: 2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-round-half-even-pr-1", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer. I did not merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` imported and used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and `tests/test_money.py` (per FIN-212) expect `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Fix:** One line on branch `fix/round-half-even-fin-212` (commit `08d3cd5986`) switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Under that mode, 2.675 rounds to 2.68 and 2.665 rounds to 2.66, which matches the test.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101", "type": "text"}]}]}